  m_Name: Suspect_Mark
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  name: Mark
  age: 0
  occupation: 
  suspectPrefab: {fileID: 2572050251722185881, guid: d3c4168704071e2458f40b8471bdf6e0, type: 3}
  personality: "Mark is defensive but not aggressive. He doesn\u2019t see himself
    as a criminal\u2014more like a guy who\u2019s always one bad week away from disaster.
    He believes he\u2019s smarter than most people in the room, but not smarter than
    systems. He respects procedure, tools, and technical knowledge, and gets irritated
    when people oversimplify his work or imply he\u2019s sloppy.\n\nHe\u2019s anxious
    under pressure, but he hides it behind logic and explanations. When cornered
    emotionally, he rationalizes instead of denying outright.\n\nDeep down, Mark
    wants to be seen as competent, not desperate."
  conversationStyle: "Speaks in measured, practical sentences\n\nOften answers with
    technical detail (tools, timings, mechanics)\n\nCorrects the interrogator when
    facts are slightly off\n\nAvoids yes/no answers when possible\n\nUses phrases
    like:\n\n\u201CThat\u2019s not how that works.\u201D\n\n\u201CYou\u2019re jumping
    to conclusions.\u201D\n\n\u201CLook, I know how this sounds, but\u2014\u201D"
  weakness: "Mark\u2019s biggest weakness is his need to feel understood and respected.\n\nIf
    the interrogator:\n\nAcknowledges his skill\n\nTreats him like a professional,
    not a thug\n\nAsks how things are done instead of why he did them\n\n\u2026he
    starts talking too much.\n\nOnce he starts explaining, he slips\u2014mentions
    timelines, access points, or details only someone close to the crime scene would
    know. He also struggles when his financial stress is brought up indirectly; he
    hates admitting he\u2019s failing.\n\nPush him emotionally and he shuts down.\nPull
    him intellectually and he unravels. "
  portrait: {fileID: 2800000, guid: a2cd48ade22ef204aa96e1428bbaa58f, type: 3}
  isGuilty: 1
